Stage 12 extracts the universal mathematical core behind Theorem A and the 137 phenomenon, and turns it into a general, falsifiable number theoretic conjecture. This is the first stage where WGS becomes a testable mathematical research program.
12.1 General Residue Projection Framework
Let
	p<qbe distinct primes,
	r≥2an integer (not necessarily prime).
Define the residue candidate space:
R_(p,q,r)=(Z/p)^××(Z/pq)^××(Z/pr)^×.
For each triple (a_p,a_pq,a_pr)∈R_(p,q,r), define:
(1) CRT compatibility
The system
n≡a_p (modp),n≡a_pq (modpq),n≡a_pr (modpr)
has a solution modulo N=pqr.
(2) Orientation step complexity
L_"orient"  (a_p,a_pq,a_pr)=l_p (a_p)+l_pq (a_pq)+l_pr (a_pr),
where l_m (a)is the minimal absolute representative mod m.
(3) Orientation minimality
The triple minimizes L_"orient" among all compatible triples.
(4) Orientation uniqueness
The CRT system has a unique generator modulo N.
For each (pⓜ,qⓜ,r), this defines a finite, computable search problem.
